# core.autocrlf is true in this environment, and git only auto-detects a file
# as binary when it finds a NUL byte early on. A PDF often has none, so it was
# treated as text: line endings were rewritten and invalid bytes replaced with
# U+FFFD, which silently destroyed the résumé. Declare binaries explicitly.

* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.svgz  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
